// A case's `given`: the function it names must be a setup -- a function in the
// build that returns void -- because the harness calls it and has nothing to
// compare its result with. It takes as many parameters as the case passes it
// literals: none for a bare `given NAME`, one per argument of
// `given NAME(LIT, ...)` (args.id). Decided from the case and the declaration
// it names, so a setup that is not one is an error at the case's line rather
// than C that does not compile.

fit_given(int i) {
  string[] setups = str_split((import casegiven)[i], " ");
  int si = 0;
  while(si < len(setups)) {
    if(setups[si] != "") {
      given_fn(i, si, setups[si]);
    }
    si = si + 1;
  }
} return void;
given impcase_empty (0):() then calls given_fn:[0]
